[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMCBOOT-15
TITLE: Flash Memory Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware can both erase and write to the flash memory of the microcontroller. The flash
memory of the microcontroller is organized into sectors and pages. Each sector is comprised of a
given number of pages, and each page is 512 bytes in size. When the firmware receives an ‘erase’
command from the PC, it will erase several pages in flash memory which have been predesignated
for application memory. For writing to flash, the communication protocol can transmit
512 bytes for each flash page size. As such, the firmware simply writes each page with data
provided by the PC write command.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-3
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-4
  ROLE: Refines

